1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,660
Overnight, hackers pushed supermarket fridges
黑客一夜之间，

2
00:00:02,660 --> 00:00:04,090
to fifty degrees Celsius.
把超市冰箱烧到了五十度。

3
00:00:04,090 --> 00:00:04,840
Fifty degrees.
五十度，

4
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:06,870
Hotter than a car in the summer sun.
比三伏天的车里还热。

5
00:00:06,870 --> 00:00:10,970
According to AP, about seven hundred French supermarkets were hit in October,
据美联社，十月份法国约七百家超市中招，

6
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:12,580
out of roughly ten thousand.
一共才一万家左右。

7
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:14,600
Late October, a new wave hit Europe.
十月底，欧洲又来一波，

8
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:17,230
Reportedly chains in Belgium and Ireland too.
据报道比利时、爱尔兰的连锁店也遭殃。

9
00:00:17,230 --> 00:00:18,360
Today's brain teaser:
今天的烧脑问题：

10
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:21,340
a fridge makes cold, so how can it turn into an oven?
冰箱是制冷的，凭啥能变成烤箱？

11
00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:22,630
Meet our hero, Frosty,
先认识主角：小冰，

12
00:00:22,630 --> 00:00:23,970
a supermarket fridge.
一台超市冰柜。

13
00:00:23,970 --> 00:00:26,370
Twist one: a fridge does not make cold at all.
反转一：冰箱根本不“造冷”。

14
00:00:26,370 --> 00:00:27,880
There is no such stuff as cold.
世上没有“冷”这种东西，

15
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:29,810
There is only more heat or less heat.
只有热多热少。

16
00:00:29,810 --> 00:00:32,000
Cold is just molecules jiggling slowly.
冷，不过是分子晃得慢；

17
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,430
Heat is the same molecules jiggling fast.
热，是同样的分子晃得快。

18
00:00:34,430 --> 00:00:35,160
A fridge's job
冰箱干的活，

19
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:37,370
is to throw heat from inside to outside.
是把热从里面赶到外面。

20
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:38,570
It is like a bouncer,
它像夜店门口的保安，

21
00:00:38,570 --> 00:00:41,140
showing heat out the back door, one by one.
把热一个个请出后门。

22
00:00:41,140 --> 00:00:43,590
Don't believe it? Touch the back of your fridge.
不信摸摸冰箱背后：

23
00:00:43,590 --> 00:00:44,210
It's warm.
是热的。

24
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:46,060
In fact, a fridge heats your kitchen.
其实冰箱一直在给厨房加热，

25
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:48,760
It dumps the food's heat, plus its own motor's heat.
吐出的是食物的热，加上电机自己的热。

26
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:48,970
How?
怎么赶？

27
00:00:48,970 --> 00:00:51,710
With a fluid that keeps moving, called refrigerant.
靠一种会“跑”的液体，叫制冷剂。

28
00:00:51,710 --> 00:00:52,770
Inside, it boils off
它在里面蒸发，

29
00:00:52,770 --> 00:00:53,840
and soaks up heat.
把热吸走。

30
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:54,450
Like sweat:
就像你出汗，

31
00:00:54,450 --> 00:00:56,470
when it evaporates, you cool down.
汗一蒸发，身上就凉了。

32
00:00:56,470 --> 00:00:58,000
Then the compressor squeezes it,
压缩机再把它压紧，

33
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,900
and the coils out back dump the heat.
在背后的管子里把热吐出去。

34
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:00,730
Round and round.
一圈又一圈，

35
00:01:00,730 --> 00:01:02,370
The bouncer never clocks out.
保安一直在加班。

36
00:01:02,370 --> 00:01:04,550
So, open the fridge to cool your kitchen?
所以开着冰箱门给厨房降温？

37
00:01:04,550 --> 00:01:06,040
The room only gets warmer.
只会越开越热。

38
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:08,940
Twist two: the bouncer takes orders from a computer.
反转二：保安是听电脑指挥的。

39
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:11,570
Supermarket fridges are linked to a control system.
超市的冰柜连着一套控制系统，

40
00:01:11,570 --> 00:01:13,590
You can set the temperature remotely.
远程就能调温度。

41
00:01:13,590 --> 00:01:17,420
According to AP, the software was from Danfoss, a Danish company.
据美联社，系统来自丹麦的丹佛斯公司，

42
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:20,200
Most hit systems were old, no longer updated.
中招的多是老设备，早就不再更新。

43
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:21,950
The lock was broken and never fixed,
门锁坏了没人修，

44
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:24,020
so hackers slipped in over the internet.
黑客就从网上溜了进来。

45
00:01:24,020 --> 00:01:25,930
Like leaving your key under the doormat,
像把家门钥匙压在门垫下，

46
00:01:25,930 --> 00:01:27,620
then posting your address online.
再把地址贴到网上。

47
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:29,260
Why put a fridge online at all?
冰柜为啥要上网？

48
00:01:29,260 --> 00:01:32,490
So one person can watch hundreds of stores from one screen.
好让一个人在一块屏幕上，盯住几百家店。

49
00:01:32,490 --> 00:01:34,350
So how did they reach fifty degrees?
那怎么烧到五十度？

50
00:01:34,350 --> 00:01:35,670
This part is our guess.
这一步，我们只能推测。

51
00:01:35,670 --> 00:01:37,470
Fridges actually contain heaters,
冰柜里本来就有加热丝，

52
00:01:37,470 --> 00:01:38,570
for melting frost.
用来化霜。

53
00:01:38,570 --> 00:01:40,800
Turn the bouncer off and leave the heaters on,
要是保安被关掉、加热丝一直开着，

54
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:42,670
and the fridge becomes a small oven.
冰柜就成了一个小烤箱。

55
00:01:42,670 --> 00:01:44,850
Reportedly some stores even had fires.
据报道，有的店还冒了火，

56
00:01:44,850 --> 00:01:47,150
The cause is still being investigated.
起因还在调查。

57
00:01:47,150 --> 00:01:49,800
Twist three, the scariest part is not the heat.
反转三，最吓人的不是热，

58
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:50,990
It is the bacteria.
是细菌。

59
00:01:50,990 --> 00:01:54,820
The USDA calls four to sixty degrees Celsius the danger zone.
美国农业部说，四度到六十度是“危险区”。

60
00:01:54,820 --> 00:01:56,540
In that zone, bacteria can double
在这个区间，细菌最快

61
00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:57,910
in about twenty minutes.
大约二十分钟翻一倍。

62
00:01:57,910 --> 00:01:59,730
One becomes two, two become four.
一个变两个，两个变四个，

63
00:01:59,730 --> 00:02:02,180
Overnight, that is an astronomical number.
一夜就是天文数字。

64
00:02:02,180 --> 00:02:03,880
A doubling every twenty minutes
二十分钟翻一倍，

65
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:06,250
is seventy-two doublings a day, on paper.
一天就是七十二次翻倍，这是纸上算的。

66
00:02:06,250 --> 00:02:08,350
So meat and milk that sat warm overnight
所以热过一夜的肉和奶，

67
00:02:08,350 --> 00:02:09,620
have to be thrown out.
只能扔掉。

68
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:11,140
Cold doesn't kill bacteria.
冷其实不杀细菌，

69
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:12,780
It just puts them to sleep.
只是让它们“冬眠”。

70
00:02:12,780 --> 00:02:14,640
That's why frozen meat, once thawed,
所以冻肉一化开，

71
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:16,880
lets the bacteria wake up and grow again.
细菌就醒过来接着长。

72
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:18,410
When the bouncer clocks out,
保安一下班，

73
00:02:18,410 --> 00:02:20,010
the bacteria throw a party.
细菌就开派对。

74
00:02:20,010 --> 00:02:23,780
Fine print: seven hundred stores and fifty degrees come from news reports.
友情提示：七百家、五十度来自新闻报道；

75
00:02:23,780 --> 00:02:26,250
How the heaters were switched on is our guess.
加热丝怎么被打开，是我们的推测。

76
00:02:26,250 --> 00:02:29,660
France's finance minister said food supply was never at risk.
法国财长说，食品供应没有风险。

77
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:32,390
According to AP, the advice from Danfoss is boring:
据美联社，丹佛斯的建议很朴素：

78
00:02:32,390 --> 00:02:34,980
keep it updated, and put it behind a firewall.
及时更新，再加一道防火墙。

79
00:02:34,980 --> 00:02:37,000
So how does a fridge become an oven?
所以，冰箱凭啥变烤箱？

80
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,310
It never made cold. It only moves heat.
因为它从来不造冷，只会搬热。

81
00:02:39,310 --> 00:02:40,970
The cold was never in the fridge.
冷，从来不在冰箱里。

82
00:02:40,970 --> 00:02:42,980
It was just heat, shown the door.
它只是热，被请出了门。

